course: dictionary
lesson: 7723
title: Puddles
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A puddle is a small pool of water on the ground, often left after rain. Children love jumping in puddles in wellies, but a puddle can also hide danger. You will meet the word in many places, so learn to spot its clues.
explain: «Deep or flooded puddles can hide holes, drains and sharp things.» The sentence tells you that you cannot see what is under the water. So a puddle that looks harmless may not be safe.
explain: The word can be shared across languages. «Kalyuzha» means puddle in Russian, and «ne liz u kalyuzhu!» means «don't go in the puddle!». Context helps here too: the warning tells you what the word means.
fact: A puddle is a small pool of water (or other liquid) on the ground, often after rain.
fact: «Kalyuzha» means puddle in Russian.
fact: Puddles can hide holes, drains and sharp things, so they are not always safe to play in.
fact: Floodwater is much bigger than a puddle, and you must never walk or play in it.
fact: Puddles dry up because the water evaporates, and they dry faster in sun and wind.
exercise: «Deep or flooded puddles can hide holes, drains and sharp things.» What can a deep puddle hide? | Clean pebbles | Sweets and crisps | *Holes, drains and sharp things | Birds and butterflies
exercise: A friend says «kalyuzha» is Russian. What does it mean? | Snowman | Sunshine | Umbrella | *Puddle
exercise: «When it rains, you stand back from the kerb, because passing cars splash water from the puddles.» Why should you stand back? | *To keep dry from splashing cars | To get a better look at the cars | To catch the rain in your hands | To jump into the puddle
test: Is floodwater a puddle? | Yes, any water on the ground is a puddle | Yes, but only when it is warm | No, because puddles are always blue | *No, it is much bigger, and you must never walk or play in it
test: Puddles dry up faster in sun and wind. What makes a puddle shrink? | The puddle grows bigger | The water turns into soup | *The water evaporates | The puddle freezes into a lake
exam: What is the safest thing to do with a puddle near a road? | *Stand back from the kerb, because passing cars can splash you | Jump in it as hard as you can | Dig a hole in the middle of it | Drink from it to see the taste
